# Project: [Your Python Project Name]

## Memory Usage Instructions
CRITICAL: Use .agent-memory/ folder for persistent notes between sessions.

- Read .agent-memory/session-notes.md at the START of each session
- Update .agent-memory/session-notes.md with progress and decisions
- Store context in .agent-memory/context.md for complex tasks
- Store ADRs in .agent-memory/adr/ directory

## Project Goal
[Describe what you're building in 1-2 sentences]

## Tech Stack
- **Python**: 3.12+ (managed via uv)
- **Package Manager**: uv (fast Python package installer and resolver)
- **Linting**: ruff (fast Python linter)
- **Type Checking**: mypy (static type checker)
- **Testing**: pytest (testing framework)
- **Formatting**: ruff format (code formatter)
- **Virtual Environment**: uv venv

## Project Structure
```
[project-name]/
├── pyproject.toml          # Project configuration and dependencies
├── uv.lock                 # Locked dependencies (auto-generated)
├── src/
│   └── [package-name]/
│       ├── __init__.py
│       └── [modules].py
├── tests/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── test_[modules].py
├── .ruff.toml              # Ruff configuration
├── .mypy.ini               # Mypy configuration (optional)
├── .env                    # Environment variables (not committed)
└── .agent-memory/          # Agent memory (auto-created)
    ├── session-notes.md
    ├── context.md
    └── adr/
```

## Development Commands

### Dependency Management (uv)
```bash
# Create virtual environment
uv venv

# Activate virtual environment
source .venv/bin/activate  # Unix
.venv\Scripts\activate     # Windows

# Add dependencies
uv add [package]           # Production dependency
uv add --dev [package]     # Development dependency

# Install dependencies
uv sync

# Update dependencies
uv lock
```

### Code Quality
```bash
# Lint (ruff)
uv run ruff check .

# Fix linting issues
uv run ruff check . --fix

# Format (ruff)
uv run ruff format .

# Type check (mypy)
uv run mypy src/

# All quality checks
uv run ruff check . && uv run ruff format . --check && uv run mypy src/
```

### Testing
```bash
# Run tests
uv run pytest

# Run tests with coverage
uv run pytest --cov=[package-name]

# Run specific test file
uv run pytest tests/test_[file].py -v

# Run tests with detailed output
uv run pytest -vvs
```

### Development Workflow
```bash
# Start with clean environment
uv sync

# Run development server
uv run [your-main-script].py

# Run with debugger
uv run python -m pdb [script].py
```

